{"id": 25, "ts": 1781177894.07334, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I appreciate James\u2019s clarification on Candidate\u202fD. While D\u2019s concentration, problem\u2011solving and sense of responsibility are strong, the added detail that he is perceived as a \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d with a \u201chot temper\u201d deepens the concern about his leadership style and its impact on crew cooperation. In a long\u2011distance cockpit, a temperamental, over\u2011confident pilot can quickly erode the collaborative environment we need for safety\u2011critical decision\u2011making.\nCompared with Candidate\u202fB, whose uncooperative moments are noted but not described as temperament\u2011driven, Candidate\u202fD now appears riskier on the crew\u2011cooperation front. Candidate\u202fC, on the other hand, remains 100\u202f% reliable, consistently creates a positive crew atmosphere, and makes correct decisions quickly\u2014core attributes for our role. Although C has communication and egocentricity concerns, these are development areas that can be addressed through training, and they do not outweigh his proven reliability and decision speed.\nTherefore, I continue to recommend **Candidate\u202fC** as the best overall fit for the long\u2011distance pilot position."}
