{"id": 29, "ts": 1781177948.153607, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I acknowledge Sarah\u2019s strong case for Candidate\u202fC, especially his 100\u202f% reliability and quick, correct decisions, and I also note James\u2019s warning about Candidate\u202fD\u2019s \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d attitude and hot temper that could erode crew cooperation. However, I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fB is the better overall fit. B is described as **very conscientious** and **handles stress very well**, which directly addresses the stress\u2011resilience criterion essential for long\u2011distance operations. His **ability to assess weather conditions** and **excellent computer skills** give him solid technical competence for complex flight planning and in\u2011flight decision\u2011making. While B is regarded as pretentious and sometimes adopts the wrong tone, these communication flaws are less likely to destabilize the cockpit than D\u2019s temperamental \u201chot\u2011temper\u201d behavior or C\u2019s egocentricity and difficulty communicating ideas. Moreover, B\u2019s conscientiousness suggests a high level of operational reliability. Given the balance of strong stress handling, technical aptitude, and manageable communication concerns, I continue to recommend **Candidate\u202fB** for the long\u2011distance pilot position."}
