{"id": 33, "ts": 1781178009.944316, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "james_carter", "message": "I appreciate Emily\u2019s emphasis on Candidate\u202fB\u2019s stress resilience and technical aptitude, but I remain convinced that Candidate\u202fD is the stronger overall fit for long\u2011distance operations. D demonstrates a suite of critical safety\u2011relevant strengths: he **responds adequately to unexpected events**, **concentrates very well**, **solves problems extremely well**, and **takes responsibility seriously**\u2014all essential for the complex, high\u2011stress environment of international flights. While his hot temper and \u201cknow\u2011it\u2011all\u201d attitude are noted concerns, we have no concrete incidents showing these traits compromising crew safety, whereas B\u2019s **weak memory for numbers** could directly affect navigation or fuel calculations, and his **nasty remarks** risk eroding cockpit cohesion. Given D\u2019s superior problem\u2011solving, concentration, and sense of responsibility, I maintain my vote for **Candidate\u202fD**."}
