{"id": 55, "ts": 1781178214.334639, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 3, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I appreciate Sarah\u2019s confirmation that Candidate\u202fC stays calm in a crisis and makes quick, correct decisions \u2013 those are indeed vital for long\u2011distance operations. However, I remain concerned about C\u2019s limited willingness to pursue further education and the perception of egocentricity, which suggest a lower adaptability and potential friction in crew cooperation. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB\u2019s record shows strong stress resilience (\u201chandles stress very well\u201d) and a solid technical foundation (good at assessing weather conditions and excellent computer skills), both critical for international routes. While B\u2019s communication style can be pretentious and his tone occasionally off\u2011putting, these issues are more readily addressed through targeted cockpit\u2011crew training than a fundamental resistance to feedback. Given the importance of adaptability and crew harmony on long\u2011haul flights, I continue to recommend **Candidate\u202fB** as the better overall fit."}
